# Local operational courts: local-only working roots, evidence environments,
# interpreters and tooling estates that live on this machine and are deliberately
# never committed.
#
# Root-anchored with a leading slash so this matches ONLY the top-level
# LOCAL_COURTS/ directory and cannot mask a same-named directory nested anywhere
# else in the tree.
#
# This is consistent with existing repository law rather than in conflict with it:
# HQ_HANDOFF/DECISION_LEDGER.jsonl already records that the qualified interpreter
# "resolves under the untracked LOCAL_COURTS path so it is genuinely uncommitted".
# At the time of this rule LOCAL_COURTS/ contained zero tracked files, so adding it
# untracked nothing and removed nothing from tracking. Paths inside LOCAL_COURTS
# remain bound live working roots referenced by HQ_HANDOFF and are unaffected by
# git's ignore rules; they are filesystem paths, not repository entries.
#
# This rule only stops git from treating several GiB of machine-local state as
# untracked noise. It is NOT a durability mechanism for that content, and it must
# never be read as authority to delete anything under LOCAL_COURTS/.
/LOCAL_COURTS/
